The NA62 experiment at CERN has achieved significant sensitivity to the $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u \overline{
u}$ decay by collecting and analyzing a large dataset from $10^{11}$ charged kaon decays. This study focuses on demonstrating the experiment's capability to detect the process with an efficiency of $81.1 \pm 0.4\%$ and an angular resolution of $2.4 \pm 0.1$ mm. This achievement enables the detection of two potential leptonic decay modes: $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u \overline{
u}$ and $K^+ 	o \pi^+ \mu^+ \mu^-$. Furthermore, the experiment reports its current constraints on the ratio of decay rates $\mathcal{R}_{K^+} = \Gamma(K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u \overline{
u}) / \Gamma(K_L 	o \pi^0 
u \overline{
u})$ and makes significant improvements to the absolute branching ratio of $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u \overline{
u}$ by a factor of 2.3.
